.TH "acwm-greeter" "1" "2026-11-17" "acwm-greeter @VERSION@" "acwm-greeter manual"

.SH NAME
acwm-greeter \- greetd greeter client for acwm

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBacwm-greeter\fP [\fB\-h\fP | \fB\-\-help\fP]

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBacwm-greeter\fP is a standalone greeter client implementing the
.B greetd
IPC protocol (JSON over \fB$GREETD_SOCK\fP). It renders a minimal
username/password overlay as a layer-shell surface and hands the
authenticated session back to greetd, which starts the user's session
command from \fBgreetd\fR(1)'s configuration.

It is intended to run inside the \fBacwm\fP greeter session: greetd starts
acwm as the greeter compositor, and the greeter user's acwm config starts
\fBacwm-greeter\fR via `exec_once`. See
.B docs/configuration/greetd.md
in the acwm source for a complete setup.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GREETD_SOCK
Path to the greetd IPC socket (set by greetd). Required.
.TP
.B ACWM_GREETER_FONT
Pango font description for the UI (default `sans 11`).

.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Return
continue (submit username/password)
.TP
.B Escape
cancel the current authentication attempt
.TP
.B Ctrl+U
clear the input field

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR acwm (1),
.BR greetd (1),
.BR greetd-ipc (7)
